    s__CATALYTIC(py_str("A catalytic converter is the box in the exhaust that turns the harmful gases into harmless ones: carbon monoxide, unburnt fuel and nitrogen oxides go in, and carbon dioxide, water and nitrogen come out, over a honeycomb coated in platinum, palladium and rhodium. It has no moving parts and normally lasts the life of the car, but it only works once it is hot, so most of its cleaning happens after the first couple of miles. It is destroyed by a misfire, by burning oil or coolant, and by leaded fuel or the wrong additive, and it is stolen for those three metals - a car that suddenly gets much louder has usually had it cut out, which is a garage job, not something to drive on."));
    s_MIST_REPLY(py_str("Clear the screen before you set off, because it is a legal requirement: front demist on, air conditioning on (it dries the air), heat up and the air on fresh rather than recirculate. A clean inside windscreen stops the mist coming back; shaving foam polished off works for a week."));
