    s_OIL_OVERFILL(py_str("A little over the top mark is not a disaster - the level is read cold on level ground, so a warm engine can show high for a few minutes - but well over it, or smoke and rough running, means drain some out before you drive far: too much oil foams, the crank whips it into the breather and the seals leak. A garage drains a bit from the sump plug in minutes, and a suction pump from the top is the no-spanner way."));
    s_TYRE_PRESSURE(py_str("Find the right pressures on the sticker inside the driver's door frame or the fuel flap, not on the tyre, and check them cold before you drive: warm tyres read a few psi high. Most cars want about 30 to 35 psi, a bit more when fully loaded. Top up every couple of weeks, because under-inflated tyres wear the edges, cost fuel and make the car feel vague."));
